msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mavlink-rcinput.rst:12
#: ca6f978b7d6742d89c527a60f30c659d
msgid ":ref:`RC Input Channel Mapping (aka RCMAP) <copter:common-rcmap>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mavlink-rcinput.rst:13
#: b9d5e0ce3fd24cff8a6ef6d9b8ca3499
msgid ":ref:`Auxiliary Functions <copter:common-auxiliary-functions>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mavlink-rcinput.rst:15
#: c0c877d9d52748afaaf75f90fef03917
msgid "The autopilot will ignore the RC input messages if the sender's system id does not match the autopilot's :ref:`MAV_GCS_SYSID <MAV_GCS_SYSID>` and :ref:`MAV_OPTIONS <MAV_OPTIONS>` = 1"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mavlink-rcinput.rst:17
#: 923d5e653cd84a6f9620a0fbd503e4a0
msgid "RC input via MAVlink typically results in a laggy response caused by telemetry system lag and/or bandwidth limitations (these messages normally share bandwidth with other MAVLink messages passed between GCS and the vehicle)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mavlink-rcinput.rst:19
#: 7a73e2bb25b64d2782af126ada26eb21
msgid "The Pilot's RC inputs can be monitored by the GCS or companion computer via the `RC_CHANNELS <https://mavlink.io/en/messages/common.html#RC_CHANNELS>`__ message"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mavlink-rcinput.rst:22
#: 35f309b02ac34e27812947ff96d16905
msgid "RC_CHANNELS_OVERRIDE"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mavlink-rcinput.rst:24
#: c1e29130decc42528cf62b04d2641354
msgid "The `RC_CHANNELS_OVERRIDE <https://mavlink.io/en/messages/common.html#RC_CHANNELS_OVERRIDE>`__ message allows setting the PWM equivalent value for each channel. This is normally a value between 1000 and 2000 but ArduPilot's RC input library uses the RCx_MIN, RCx_MAX and RCx_TRIM parameters to scale the input.  Note though that these parameters are normally set by the user during the RC Calibration stage."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mavlink-rcinput.rst:27
#: 32fe2c84cf6f420a8d1e50ee9997c6b1
msgid "If both a regular transmitter (e.g. Futaba, Spektrum, etc) which sends actually PWM values and a MAVLink enabled RC input system (sending messages via one of the message listed on this page) then care should be taken to ensure the RCx_MIN/MAX ranges are consistent between the two systems. If the MAVLink RC input stops, ArduPilot falls back to regular RC input within a few seconds.  This timeout is configurable using the :ref:`RC_OVERRIDE_TIME <copter:RC_OVERRIDE_TIME>` parameter."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mavlink-rcinput.rst:30
#: 04cf52293fc7467a822f8aef37dace54
msgid "Be careful not to change the flight mode inadvertently.  By default either channel 5 or channel 8 (depending upon the vehicle type) is used to set the flight mode but this can be disabled by setting :ref:`FLTMODE_CH <copter:FLTMODE_CH>` or :ref:`MODE_CH <rover:MODE_CH>` to 0"
msgstr ""

